Bound the app-name table, and size it for this feed's signature set

init_app_name_table() fills a fixed 1024-entry global array with one row per
line of the feature file and never checks the index:

    app_name_info_t app_name_table[MAX_SUPPORT_APP_NUM];   /* 1024 */
    ...
    app_name_table[g_app_count].id = app_id;
    strcpy(app_name_table[g_app_count].name, app_name);
    g_app_count++;                       /* no bound, ever */

Signature 1025 onward writes past the end of the array. The process does not
die there -- it keeps running while corrupting whatever follows in BSS, and
segfaults around 1098 entries. That delay is what makes this expensive to
find: bisecting the database shows a clean cliff at 1098/1099 that looks like
a deliberate capacity limit, removing the signature at the boundary does not
help, and the fault surfaces during traffic rather than at load.

Confirmed by construction: a file of 1188 signatures built only from upstream's
own entries, using upstream's class numbering, crashes identically. The
trigger is the row count alone. Nothing about the ids, the classes or the
feature format is involved.

Two changes, because either alone is insufficient:

- The bound check makes an oversized database degrade to partial coverage with
  a log line instead of corrupting memory. That is correct for any size of
  table and is the part worth keeping regardless.
- 4096 sizes the table for the ~1,349-signature database this package ships.
  app_name_info_t is {int id; char name[64]}, so the array grows from about
  70KB to 280KB, which is not material on these targets.

Without this, the feed's own signature database cannot be loaded at all: the
engine silently runs on upstream's 228 entries instead.

--- a/open-app-filter/src/appfilter_config.h
+++ b/open-app-filter/src/appfilter_config.h
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 #define __APPFILTER_CONFIG_H__
 #include <uci.h>
 
-#define MAX_SUPPORT_APP_NUM 1024
+#define MAX_SUPPORT_APP_NUM 4096
 #define MAX_CLASS_NAME_LEN 32
 #define MAX_PARAM_LIST_LEN 1024
 
--- a/open-app-filter/src/appfilter_config.c
+++ b/open-app-filter/src/appfilter_config.c
@@ -446,6 +446,11 @@
         memset(app_name, 0x0, sizeof(app_name));
         strncpy(app_info_buf, line_buf, pos1 - line_buf);
         sscanf(app_info_buf, "%d %s", &app_id, app_name);
+        if (g_app_count >= MAX_SUPPORT_APP_NUM) {
+            printf("feature file has more than %d apps; ignoring the remainder\n",
+                   MAX_SUPPORT_APP_NUM);
+            break;
+        }
         app_name_table[g_app_count].id = app_id;
         strcpy(app_name_table[g_app_count].name, app_name);
         g_app_count++;
